# UI Style Contract

This example UI is token-driven. Colors, surfaces, borders, shadows, and motion should come from `src/index.css` and the Tailwind theme mappings. Components should not hardcode palette values or invent a parallel visual system.

## Token-first styling

All application UI colors, surfaces, borders, and text states **MUST** come from the semantic token system exposed by `src/index.css`.

Use semantic classes such as:

- `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`
- `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`
- `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`
- `bg-success/15`, `text-success`
- `bg-warning/15`, `text-warning`
- `bg-danger/15`, `text-danger`

### DO

```tsx
<div className="bg-background text-foreground border-border shadow-sm" />
<Badge className="bg-success/15 text-success">Active</Badge>
<button className="border-border bg-muted text-foreground">Save</button>
```

### DON'T

```tsx
<div className="bg-[#161618] text-[#fafafa] border-[#3a3a3f]" />
<div className="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 border-gray-700" />
<div className="rounded-none border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/10 p-3 text-red-700">Error</div>
```

## Prohibited color patterns

Raw Tailwind palette classes are **FORBIDDEN** in application code under `src/`:

```
bg-red-*    bg-emerald-*    bg-amber-*    bg-green-*    bg-yellow-*
text-red-*  text-emerald-*  text-amber-*  text-green-*  text-yellow-*
border-red-* border-emerald-* border-amber-* border-green-* border-yellow-*
```

Use semantic utilities instead. If a new semantic state appears, add or reuse a token rather than reaching for a palette class.

**Exception:** data-driven colors that come from user input or external data may use inline `style={{ backgroundColor }}` or similar when the color itself is content, not design. Keep these cases narrow and document them inline.

## Inline styles

### Forbidden

Structural styling (layout, spacing, colors, borders) via `style={{}}`.

```tsx
// ✗ Never
<div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: '16px', backgroundColor: '#1a1a1a' }}>
```

### Allowed (with justification)

Dynamic values that cannot be expressed cleanly with Tailwind classes:

```tsx
// ✓ User-provided color swatch
<div style={{ backgroundColor: tokenHexValue }} />

// ✓ Calculated dimension
<div style={{ width: `${percentage}%` }} />

// ✓ Tree depth indentation
<div style={{ paddingLeft: `${depth * 14 + 8}px` }} />
```

## Overlays and portals

- Prefer the existing shadcn/Radix overlay primitives already wired into the app (`Sheet`, `DropdownMenu`, `ScrollArea`, `Select`, etc.).
- Do not hand-roll portal plumbing in application components when an existing primitive already handles the overlay behavior.
- If a custom portal is truly unavoidable, isolate it in a reusable primitive and document why it exists.

## Typography

Both font tokens are declared in the `@theme inline` block in `src/index.css`:

- `--font-sans: 'Noto Sans Variable', sans-serif` — applied globally to `html` via `@apply font-sans` in `@layer base`.
- `--font-heading: 'Roboto Slab Variable', serif` — applied explicitly with `font-heading` where visual weight is needed.

| Element | Class | Hierarchy Role | Rationale |
|---------|-------|----------------|-----------|
| Page/section headings | `font-heading` | Title hierarchy | Roboto Slab Variable; uppercase + tracking-wide in most usages |
| UI text, labels, body | `font-sans` (default) | Body hierarchy | Noto Sans Variable; inherited via `html`; no need to apply explicitly unless overriding |
| Token paths, code | `font-mono` | Technical/code hierarchy | Monospace rhythm for paths, values, and code-like data |

- **MUST** use semantic heading levels (`<h1>` page, `<h2>` section, `<h3>` subsection).
- **SHOULD** keep headings aligned with the existing visual rhythm: `font-heading` + uppercase + `tracking-wide` where the UI already uses that pattern, not as a blanket rule everywhere.
- Do not redefine font families inline — both tokens are already wired through `@theme inline`; use the utility classes.

## Form and interaction surfaces

- Keep primary labels visible and readable.
- Use the existing primitives in `src/components/ui` instead of inventing custom wrappers unless the pattern is repeated and clearly reusable.
- Icon-only controls require `aria-label`.
- Keep error, warning, and status messaging semantic instead of embedding raw color classes in inline markup.

## Dark mode

The app supports dark tokens through the token layer in `src/index.css`.

- Do not duplicate light/dark palette values in component code.
- Prefer token classes over theme-specific branching in JSX.
- If a primitive already emits `dark:` modifiers because of its internal implementation, leave it alone; application code should not add new theme-specific color logic unless it is token-backed.

## Motion

- Use modest, purposeful transitions that match the existing primitives.
- Respect reduced motion settings.
- Avoid introducing animation libraries for simple UI feedback unless the benefit is clear.

## Enforcement

- Violations in new code **MUST** be fixed.
- Existing violations: fix when touching the file (boy scout rule).
- When unsure whether a pattern is allowed, prefer the token system — it exists to absorb these decisions centrally.

### Verification

Review touched UI files for token usage, raw palette classes, unnecessary portal plumbing, and heading hierarchy consistency.
